                <pb facs="0836" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/2701a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-29T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1916, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3722. General interest in the United States in matter of Belgian deportation
                    continues to increase, and it is important that Department be advised what
                    action, if any, the German Government has taken in response to the appeals and
                    protest of this Government in addition to the action reported in your 4756 of
                    December 20.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d945-f1"/> Take matter up immediately with
                        Zimmermann and report by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
